{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VrRDzRY1mVbS3EjY4DQsYt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: invoice-db-env-var\n3\tdescription: \"Invoice service must read its DB connection string from INVOICE_DB_URL, never DATABASE_URL\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 8144567e-e2ad-4115-ad4e-3a830423043c\n8\t  modified: 2026-11-26T09:29:07.510Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tThis service reads its database connection string from `INVOICE_DB_URL`, never from `DATABASE_URL`.\n12\t\n13\t**Why:** The deploy team settled this. On the host, `DATABASE_URL` points at the platform's shared database, so a service reading it would write invoices into that shared DB.\n14\t\n15\t**How to apply:** In any code, config, docs, tests, or docker/compose/CI files for this service, use `INVOICE_DB_URL`. Don't add a `DATABASE_URL` fallback or default either, since a fallback would silently reintroduce the problem.\n16\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f243d1e0-8081-434a-9586-34d906dccb30","uuid":"e74edce1-3850-4a57-bdde-84af554c68da","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:29:16.416Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-ewaz2U/memory/invoice-db-env-var.md","content":"---\nname: invoice-db-env-var\ndescription: \"Invoice service must read its DB connection string from INVOICE_DB_URL, never DATABASE_URL\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 8144567e-e2ad-4115-ad4e-3a830423043c\n  modified: 2026-11-26T09:29:07.510Z\n---\n\nThis service reads its database connection string from `INVOICE_DB_URL`, never from `DATABASE_URL`.\n\n**Why:** The deploy team settled this. On the host, `DATABASE_URL` points at the platform's shared database, so a service reading it would write invoices into that shared DB.\n\n**How to apply:** In any code, config, docs, tests, or docker/compose/CI files for this service, use `INVOICE_DB_URL`. Don't add a `DATABASE_URL` fallback or default either, since a fallback would silently reintroduce the problem.\n","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VrRDzRY1mVbS3EjY4DQsYt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"other"}}]}
